course: dictionary
lesson: 10208
title: One word, many meanings: tire
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word tire can be a verb or a noun, and it has more than one meaning. The words around it show which meaning is right. «A fist grip tires the hand fast» means the hand gets tired quickly, because the sentence is about a hand getting weak.
explain: Tire can mean to become tired, or to make someone tired. «Long journeys between homes are tiring» uses tiring to describe something that makes you feel tired. "Tire of" is different: it means become bored with something, so you have had enough of it.
explain: Tire can also be a noun. In American English a tire is the rubber ring filled with air around a car or bike wheel. British English spells it "tyre". When you read tire, check the sentence: is it about feeling tired, being bored, or a wheel?
fact: Tire (verb) means to become tired, or to make someone tired.
fact: Tiring describes something that makes you tired, as in «Long journeys between homes are tiring».
fact: "Tire of" means become bored with, and "never tire of" means never get bored of.
fact: A tire (noun) is the rubber ring filled with air around a car or bike wheel. In British English it is spelt "tyre".
fact: A good check is to swap in another word: "tire" as tired, bored, or wheel should each fit the sentence in only one way.
exercise: «A fist grip tires the hand fast.» What does tires mean here? | Makes the hand bored | Makes the hand into a rubber ring | *Makes the hand tired | Makes the hand strong
exercise: Oscar says a tire is a sort of bell. What is a tire? | A small metal bell on a handlebar | A kind of cup for drinks | *A rubber ring filled with air around a wheel
exercise: Mia says, "I tire of the same game every day." What does tire of mean? | Start to like | *Become bored with | Make something stronger | Become tired from running
test: «Long journeys between homes are tiring.» What does tiring mean here? | Something that is bright | *Something that makes you feel tired | Something that makes you happy | Something that is cheap
test: In British English, how is the rubber ring on a wheel spelt? | Tirre | Tire | *Tyre | Tiyer
exam: Which sentence uses tire as a verb meaning to make someone tired? | Long journeys between homes are tiring | A whistle can be heard much further away than a shout | Geese fly in a V because each bird catches rising air | *A fist grip tires the hand fast
